.TH "YAMLR-RULES" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-rules \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBRule Catalog Dashboard\fR
.PP
Displays a comprehensive table of all active semantic rules, checkers, and healers available in the current version.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr rules [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-v, --verbose\fR: Show full rationale for every rule in an extra column.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--output=json\fR: Export rule database as structured JSON.
.SH "COLUMNS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBID\fR: The unique Rule ID (e.g., \fBrules/no-latest-tag\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBName\fR: Human-readable name.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBSeverity\fR: ERROR, WARNING, or INFO.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBDescription\fR: Brief summary of what the rule detects.
.SS " Global Performance Flags"
Available across all commands:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Output surgical execution timing breakdown.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing-file <FILE>\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Save performance profiling data to a JSON file.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
yamlr rules
# Lists all 50+ active rules
.RE
.fi
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
